From: surface-kit
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: Tuning files for the Surface Pro 7 sensors

Set the ov8865 and ov5693 black level (64 at 10 bits) instead of letting
the soft IPA guess it from the darkest pixels.

---
--- a/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build	2026-10-06 20:58:40.473001956 +0200
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build	2026-10-06 20:58:40.480437253 +0200
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
 
 conf_files = files([
+    'ov5693.yaml',
+    'ov8865.yaml',
     'uncalibrated.yaml',
 ])
 
--- a/src/ipa/simple/data/ov5693.yaml	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/data/ov5693.yaml	2026-10-06 20:58:40.478437260 +0200
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
+%YAML 1.1
+---
+# Surface Pro 7. The sensor's black level target is fixed at 64 (10-bit);
+# without it the soft IPA guesses one from the darkest 2% of the image,
+# which in scenes without real black skews brightness and colour balance.
+version: 1
+algorithms:
+  - BlackLevel:
+      blackLevel: 4096
+  - Awb:
+  - Adjust:
+  - Agc:
+...
--- a/src/ipa/simple/data/ov8865.yaml	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/data/ov8865.yaml	2026-10-06 20:58:40.475437271 +0200
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
+%YAML 1.1
+---
+# Surface Pro 7. The sensor's black level target is fixed at 64 (10-bit);
+# without it the soft IPA guesses one from the darkest 2% of the image,
+# which in scenes without real black skews brightness and colour balance.
+version: 1
+algorithms:
+  - BlackLevel:
+      blackLevel: 4096
+  - Awb:
+  - Adjust:
+  - Agc:
+...
